WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.235
-Your mom -- I know she's
a big fan of your work.

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
She still come on set?
Still visits you?

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.605
-Oh, yeah. Kay Mac still
comes to sets. She still --

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
Her dream was to be
on "Golden Girls."

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
-Somehow.

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:11.878 line:92%
-That's a very noble dream.

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:14.647 line:92%
-Hey, with a capital "N."

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:15.215 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And so she --

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:19.119
I guess when she got around 70,
she decided, "You know what?

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe I'm not as limber
as I need to be

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
for 'Golden Girls' anymore.
I'm gonna start --

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:25.291 size:84% position:42%
When I get to Matthew's
sets, I'm going to make
sure that I find..."

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
She always comes and goes,
"Who's the one with the money?

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:29.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
Who's the one
that can get things done?"

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:32.632
And I'm like, "That guy over
there or that woman over there."

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.200 line:92%
And she'll go corner them.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.402 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And for about 12 years,

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:40.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
she had a pitch to
so-said "money-man" producer.

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:45.612
She had this great idea.
Listen to this. Brilliant.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:49.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We need to remake
'The Graduate.'

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:51.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll play the
Anne Bancroft role.

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:53.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
Matthew will be
the Dustin Hoffman role."

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:55.522
The first reaction's like,
"But don't you know...?"

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:58.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Mom always says, "Oh,
it's not that big of a deal.

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:00.427 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I've seen it before."

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:01.061 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:02.829
-Still unmade. It's one
of those unmade classics.

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:05.598
-Unmade, and, I mean, there was
a couple times people were like,

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:08.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
"That could make --
That could make some money."

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:12.605
So she stopped doing that at 82.
She's now 86.

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
She hasn't pitched
to any of the producers.

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:15.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know what
she's got on her mind now.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:19.179 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah, well, maybe this
"Golden Girls" thing
will come back around.

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:20.580 line:92%
You never know. You're --

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to know if this
is a true story.

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:23.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your father had a cockatiel?
-Yeah.

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:25.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Am I saying that right?
-Yeah, cockatiel.

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:27.187 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-And there was a story

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:29.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
about a very harrowing evening
with the cockatiel.

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:34.194
-Yeah. This was a summer
where I was living with my dad.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:35.261 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Mom was not around.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:38.398
I thought she was on an extended
vacation in Florida.

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:39.899 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Now I understand

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.734 size:88% position:44%
they were in the middle
of their second divorce.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your parents
got divorced twice.

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:44.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Divorced twice,
married three times.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
-So this was a long summer

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.474 size:75% position:38%
where I just thought
Mom was on vacation.

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:50.944
So I'm living with my dad,
and we had this cockatiel.

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:52.278 line:92%
And I would let it fly freely.

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:55.915
Well, he came home from work
one day, and then I came in.

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was looking
for his cockatiel.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:58.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
Where is it? Where is it?
Where is it?

00:01:58.218 --> 00:02:00.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not in the cage.
It's not anywhere to be found.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:02.455 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Go in the bathroom,

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:05.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was circling
in the bottom of the toilet.

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.727 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Not moving. Done.

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:08.928 line:92%
-How does that even happen?

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:11.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I guess it flew in
and got under the rim.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:11.898 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay, yeah.

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:13.566
-Couldn't see, couldn't get out.
Over and over and over.

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:16.002
Just laid in the water,
got soaking wet. I guess.

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:19.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
Being a cockatiel
detective expert.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:21.274 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:23.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, anyway, it's float--
And it's circling.

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:26.679 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-"CSI: Birds."

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:30.416 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Coming to ya. 8:00 p.m.

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:33.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, oh, Dad immediately
starts weeping

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:35.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
and gets down,
drops to two knees,

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:38.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
and pulls this soaking-wet
cockatiel bird out.

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:41.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember these tears
going down his face

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:42.529 line:92%
and my dad holding this wet bird

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:44.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then suddenly putting
the bird's mouth --

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:46.733 size:81% position:41% line:92%
his head in his mouth.

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:48.034 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And he started going --

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:48.701 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Exhales deeply ]

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:51.404 size:84% position:42%
Like, at the perfect --
My dad was a big man.

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:54.574 line:92%
6'4", 265. Big arms, big man.

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:57.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he did it with the
perfect amount of pressure

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:00.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
you would do to
a small bird that size.

00:03:00.747 --> 00:03:02.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just enough
to blow his lungs out.

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:04.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he sat there,
and he kept going --

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:04.851 line:92%
Tears were coming down his face.

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:08.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
And damned if after
about 45 seconds...

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:10.256 line:92%
the bird starts flapping.

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:12.358 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Bup-bup-bup-bup-bup...

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:13.760 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's the movie.
-That's cool.

00:03:16.663 --> 00:03:18.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's the movie.
-That's cool.

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:19.632 line:92%
-Oh, well, cheers to that.

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:21.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
And cheers to the bourbon.
And the film.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:24.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you, Seth.
-Thanks for being back.

